  "description": "ALAQEL crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P n m a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H142 Eu6 N15 O49 Zn6 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),2(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Eu1G (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2G (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu3G (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Zn1G (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2G (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3G (Zn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.488-5.025 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.01-174.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C110H146Eu6N18O61Zn6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
